hing is permitted in accordance with Nevada Department of Wildlife regulations; boat launches are available at Sand Harbor."},{id:"spring-mountain-ranch-state-park",name:"Spring Mountain Ranch State Park",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/fbc681b3552f60bc.webp",photoGallery:[],shortDescription:"Nestled in the Red Rock Canyon National Conservation Area, this historic ranch offers a unique blend of lush green pastures and dramatic desert mountain scenery.",fullDescription:"Spring Mountain Ranch State Park is a 520-acre oasis located at the base of the Wilson Cliffs. Originally established in the 1860s, the ranch has a colorful history involving early settlers, wealthy socialites, and even Hollywood stars like Vera Krupp and Howard Hughes. The park preserves historic ranch buildings, including the main ranch house, and provides a cool, green retreat from the nearby Las Vegas heat.",thingsToDo:["Guided historic ranch house tours","Picnicking in the shaded groves","Wildlife viewing","Photography of the Wilson Cliffs","Attending outdoor theater performances"],hikingTrails:[{name:"Sandstone Canyon Trail",difficulty:"Moderate",length:"2.5 miles",description:"A scenic trail that leads hikers through beautiful sandstone formations and offers panoramic views of the valley."},{name:"Overlook Trail",difficulty:"Easy",length:"0.5 miles",description:"A short, accessible path that provides a stunning vantage point of the entire ranch property and surrounding mountains."}],campingInfo:"There is no public camping available at Spring Mountain Ranch State Park; however, nearby Red Rock Canyon offers limited camping options.",wildlife:["Desert bighorn sheep","Coyotes","Mule deer","Red-tailed hawks","Jackrabbits"],visitorCenter:{name:"Spring Mountain Ranch Visitor Center",info:"Provides information on the ranch's history, local geology, and guided tour schedules.",hours:"Daily: 10:00 AM - 4:00 PM",phone:"(702) 875-4141"},hours:"8:00 AM - 4:30 PM daily",address:"6375 NV-15