ing valley."}],campingInfo:"The park offers 14 campsites suitable for tents and small RVs, available on a first-come, first-served basis with fire pits and picnic tables.",wildlife:["Mule deer","Coyotes","Golden eagles","Mountain lions","Chukar"],visitorCenter:{name:"Park Ranger Station",info:"Provides information on fossil tours, park history, and safety guidelines for the remote desert environment.",hours:"Daily: 9:00 AM - 4:00 PM",phone:"(775) 964-2440"},hours:"Open 24 hours daily for day use; camping is permitted in designated sites.",address:"2 State Park Rd, Austin, NV 89310",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Berlin-Ichthyosaur+State+Park+NV",officialWebsite:"https://parks.nv.gov/parks/berlin-ichthyosaur",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring and Fall, as summer temperatures can be extreme and winter brings heavy snow.",tips:["Bring plenty of water and supplies as the park is very remote.","Check the official website for fossil shelter tour schedules before arriving.","Ensure your vehicle has a full tank of gas before heading into the Shoshone Mountains."],nearbyAttractions:["Austin, Nevada","Toiyabe National Forest","Great Basin National Park"],entranceFees:"$5.00 per vehicle for Nevada residents, $10.00 for non-residents.",fishingBoating:"Not applicable; there are no bodies of water suitable for fishing or boating within the park."},{id:"beaver-dam-state-park",name:"Beaver Dam State Park",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/park-beaver-dam-state-park-nevada.webp",photoGallery:[],shortDescription:"A remote and rugged high-desert oasis featuring dramatic volcanic rock formations and a picturesque reservoir.",fullDescription:"Beaver Dam State Park is located in a deep, narrow canyon in the eastern part of Nevada. The park is known for its unique geology, including dramatic volcanic rock formations and the remnants of a historic dam. Visitors can explore the diverse landscape which transitions from high desert scrub to lush riparian zones along 