ark offers 28 drive-in campsites, 22 cart-in sites, and several rustic camper cabins available for reservation year-round.",wildlife:["Black bear","Moose","Bald eagle","Peregrine falcon","White-tailed deer"],visitorCenter:{name:"Tettegouche Visitor Center",info:"Features interactive exhibits on the geology, history, and ecology of the North Shore, along with a gift shop and information desk.",hours:"Daily: 9:00 AM - 5:00 PM",phone:"(218) 353-8800"},hours:"Park grounds open daily from 8:00 AM to 10:00 PM",address:"5702 Highway 61, Silver Bay, MN 55614",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Tettegouche+State+Park+MN",officialWebsite:"https://www.dnr.state.mn.us/state_parks/park.html?id=spk00278",bestTimeToVisit:"Late September to early October for spectacular fall foliage colors.",tips:["Wear sturdy hiking boots as the trails can be rocky and uneven.","Check the park website for seasonal trail closures due to mud or ice.","Bring binoculars for spotting raptors near the cliff edges."],nearbyAttractions:["Split Rock Lighthouse State Park","George H. Crosby Manitou State Park","Silver Bay","Two Harbors"],entranceFees:"Daily vehicle permit is $7.00 or an annual state park permit is $35.00.",fishingBoating:"Fishing is popular in the Baptism River for trout and along the Lake Superior shoreline; no boat ramps are available within the park."},{id:"itasca-state-park",name:"Itasca State Park",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/6768783bc73412f6.webp",photoGallery:[],shortDescription:"Home to the headwaters of the Mississippi River, Itasca State Park is Minnesota's oldest state park and a premier destination for nature lovers.",fullDescription:"Established in 1891, Itasca State Park encompasses over 32,000 acres of pristine wilderness, including the iconic headwaters where the Mississippi River begins its 2,552-mile journey to the Gulf of Mexico. The park features a diverse landscape of towering old-growth red and white pines, glacial lakes, and abundant 