ock formations and deep glacial potholes.",fullDescription:"Interstate State Park, established in 1895, is the oldest state park in Minnesota. It is renowned for the Dalles of the St. Croix, a deep gorge carved by glacial meltwater that features some of the deepest potholes in the world. The park offers a unique look into geological history with its exposed volcanic basalt flows and diverse riverine ecosystem.",thingsToDo:["Hiking along the river gorge","Rock climbing on basalt cliffs","Canoeing and kayaking the St. Croix River","Picnicking near the riverbank","Geological sightseeing of glacial potholes"],hikingTrails:[{name:"River Trail",difficulty:"Moderate",length:"1.2 miles",description:"This trail follows the edge of the St. Croix River, offering stunning views of the gorge and the unique rock formations."},{name:"Pothole Trail",difficulty:"Easy",length:"0.5 miles",description:"A short, interpretive trail that leads visitors through the park's most famous collection of glacial potholes."}],campingInfo:"The park features 37 drive-in campsites, many with electrical hookups, and several walk-in sites. Reservations are highly recommended during peak summer months.",wildlife:["White-tailed deer","Bald eagles","Wild turkeys","Various songbirds","Beavers"],visitorCenter:{name:"Interstate State Park Visitor Center",info:"The visitor center provides educational exhibits on the geology of the St. Croix River valley and the history of the park.",hours:"Daily: 9:00 AM - 4:00 PM",phone:"(651) 257-2288"},hours:"8:00 AM - 10:00 PM daily",address:"307 Milltown Rd, Taylors Falls, MN 55084",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Interstate+State+Park+Taylors+Falls+MN",officialWebsite:"https://www.dnr.state.mn.us/state_parks/park.html?id=spk00190",bestTimeToVisit:"Late spring through early autumn for hiking and water activities.",tips:["Wear sturdy hiking boots as the terrain near the gorge can be uneven and rocky.","Check the park website for seasonal rock climbing permi