ame:"Minneopa State Park Office",info:"Provides park information, maps, and educational displays about the local geology and the bison restoration project.",hours:"Daily: 8:00 AM - 4:30 PM",phone:"(507) 389-5464"},hours:"8:00 AM - 10:00 PM daily",address:"54497 Gadwall Rd, Mankato, MN 56001",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Minneopa+State+Park+MN",officialWebsite:"https://www.dnr.state.mn.us/state_parks/park.html?id=spk00237",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring for the waterfall flow or Autumn for the prairie colors.",tips:["Check the park website for bison drive closures before arriving.","Wear sturdy shoes if you plan to hike the gorge trails as they can be slippery.","Bring a camera for the waterfall, as it is one of the most photographed spots in Southern Minnesota."],nearbyAttractions:["Mankato","Sibley Park","Blue Earth County History Center","Mount Kato Ski Area"],entranceFees:"$7.00 daily vehicle permit or $35.00 annual permit.",fishingBoating:"Fishing is permitted in the Minnesota River, which borders the park, though there are no boat ramps within the park boundaries."},{id:"blue-mounds-state-park",name:"Blue Mounds State Park",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/d2196d0229c6b4db.webp",photoGallery:[],shortDescription:"Famous for its dramatic Sioux Quartzite cliffs and a roaming herd of American bison, Blue Mounds offers a unique prairie landscape in southwestern Minnesota.",fullDescription:"Blue Mounds State Park is defined by its massive outcroppings of Sioux Quartzite, which rise 100 feet above the surrounding prairie. The park preserves a significant portion of native tallgrass prairie, providing a glimpse into the landscape as it appeared before European settlement. Visitors can explore the unique geology, view the bison herd managed by the Minnesota Department of Natural Resources, and enjoy panoramic views from the cliff tops.",thingsToDo:["Bison viewing","Rock climbing","Hiking","Camping","Swimming","Bird watching"],hikingTrails:[{n