ark.",fishingBoating:"Fishing is permitted along the Yadkin River section of the park, and there is a canoe access area for paddlers to enjoy the river."},{id:"mount-mitchell-state-park",name:"Mount Mitchell State Park",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/park-mount-mitchell-state-park-north-carolina.webp",photoGallery:[],shortDescription:"Home to the highest peak east of the Mississippi River, Mount Mitchell State Park offers breathtaking panoramic views and a unique high-elevation spruce-fir forest.",fullDescription:"Established in 1915 as North Carolina's first state park, Mount Mitchell rises 6,684 feet above sea level. The park protects a rare southern Appalachian spruce-fir forest, an ecosystem more common in Canada than the southern United States. Visitors can explore the summit observation deck, which provides 360-degree views of the Blue Ridge Mountains, and learn about the mountain's history, including the legacy of Elisha Mitchell, for whom the peak is named.",thingsToDo:["Hiking to the summit observation deck","Picnicking in the high-elevation forest","Birdwatching for rare species","Photography of the Blue Ridge Mountains","Educational exhibits at the museum"],hikingTrails:[{name:"Summit Trail",difficulty:"Easy",length:"0.25 miles",description:"A short, paved path leading from the parking area to the observation deck at the highest point."},{name:"Balsam Nature Trail",difficulty:"Easy",length:"0.75 miles",description:"A loop trail that winds through the beautiful spruce-fir forest, offering a peaceful walk through the high-altitude ecosystem."}],campingInfo:"The park features a small, primitive tent-only campground with 9 sites available by reservation, typically open from May through October.",wildlife:["Northern flying squirrel","Saw-whet owl","Black bear","White-tailed deer","Junco"],visitorCenter:{name:"Mount Mitchell Visitor Center",info:"Features exhibits on the natural history, geology, and human history of the Black Mountains, 