hing","Picnicking in shaded groves","Geocaching"],hikingTrails:[{name:"Sculptured Oak Nature Trail",difficulty:"Easy",length:"0.5 miles",description:"A short, interpretive loop that winds through the maritime forest, showcasing native flora and fauna."},{name:"Yaupon Nature Trail",difficulty:"Easy",length:"0.4 miles",description:"A peaceful trail that traverses through dense thickets of yaupon holly and coastal vegetation."}],campingInfo:"The park features 278 campsites, many with water and electrical hookups, capable of accommodating RVs and tents, located just a short walk from the beach.",wildlife:["Loggerhead sea turtles","Great blue herons","Ospreys","White-tailed deer","Brown pelicans"],visitorCenter:{name:"Myrtle Beach State Park Nature Center",info:"Features interactive exhibits on local marine life, sea turtle conservation, and the park's history.",hours:"Daily: 9:00 AM - 5:00 PM",phone:"(843) 238-0874"},hours:"6:00 AM - 10:00 PM daily",address:"4401 South Kings Hwy, Myrtle Beach, SC 29575",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Myrtle+Beach+State+Park+SC",officialWebsite:"https://southcarolinaparks.com/myrtle-beach",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring and Fall for mild temperatures and fewer crowds.",tips:["Visit the pier early in the morning to catch the sunrise and avoid peak heat.","Check the park's event calendar for guided sea turtle nest walks during summer months.","Bring insect repellent if you plan to hike the nature trails, especially in the warmer months."],nearbyAttractions:["Brookgreen Gardens","Myrtle Beach Boardwalk","Huntington Beach State Park","Broadway at the Beach"],entranceFees:"$8.00 for adults, $5.00 for SC seniors, $4.00 for children ages 6-15, free for children 5 and under.",fishingBoating:"The park features a popular fishing pier with a bait and tackle shop; fishing is permitted from the pier and along the beach (outside of designated swimming areas)."},{id:"caesars-head-state-park",name:"Caesars Head State Park",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/20a9e6e604248309.webp",photoGallery:[],shortDescription:"Perched atop the Blue Ridge Escarpment, Caesars Head offers breathtaking panoramic views and access to the rugged Mountain Bridge Wilderness Area.",fullDescription:"Caesars Head State Park is a premier destination in the South Carolina Upstate, famous for its dramatic granite rock outcropping that provides sweeping views of the Blue Ridge Mountains. The park serves as the gateway to the 13,000-acre Mountain Bridge Wilderness Area, a protected corridor of diverse ecosystems, waterfalls, and challenging terrain. Geologically, the area is defined by the Blue Ridge Escarpment, where the Piedmont plateau abruptly rises to meet the mountains, creating unique microclimates and spectacular vistas.",thingsToDo:["Hiking and backpacking","Bird watching","Photography","Picnicking","Nature study"],hikingTrails:[{name:"Raven Cliff Falls Trail",difficulty:"Moderate",length:"4.0 miles round-trip",description:"A popular trail that leads to a suspension bridge overlooking the 420-foot Raven Cliff Falls."},{name:"Caesars Head Trail",difficulty:"Easy",length:"0.5 miles",description:"A short, accessible path leading directly to the famous overlook at the top of the granite dome."}],campingInfo:"Primitive backcountry camping is available within the Mountain Bridge Wilderness Area by permit only; there are no drive-up campsites at the park.",wildlife:["Black bears","Peregrine falcons","Wild turkeys","White-tailed deer","Various salamander species"],visitorCenter:{name:"Caesars Head Visitor Center",info:"The center provides trail maps, educational exhibits on local geology and wildlife, and information on the Mountain Bridge Wilderness Area.",hours:"Daily: 9:00 AM - 5:00 PM",phone:"(864) 836-6115"},hours:"Daily: 9:00 AM - 6:00 PM (Extended hours during summer)",address:"8155 Geer Hwy, Cleveland, SC 29635",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Caesars+Head+State+Park+SC",officialWebsite:"https://s